  "decisions_043_048": [
    {
      "row": "| DEC-043 (accepted 2026-09-14, 17:30 EDT: \"DEC-043 default is fine\") | 2026-09-14 | **Primary condition v3 = v2 reader + R1-56 rare-token overlap gate** (`rare_overlap_min=1`, `rare_df_max=2`): a non-learned deployment rule fixed on development streams before the freeze; removes the growth of zsRE unseen-prompt false fires with memory size (45 % \u2192 10 % at 1,000 records) at \u2264 0.01 RET-GS. Applies if the lead says nothing before the freeze. | `docs/R1_stage2_notes.md` (R1-56); `manifests/revision_v1/primary_condition_v3.json`. | Proposed by the orchestrator; the lead may keep v2. |",
      "sha256": "416a8a08074a33ce592d25c4fd25f1fa2fc4332365417edba2ef508827635caf"
    },
    {
      "row": "| DEC-044 | 2026-09-14 | **Run-matrix scope is not cut**: the lead keeps the full 240-cell v3 matrix (8 conditions \u00d7 2 datasets \u00d7 3 realizations \u00d7 5 orders, checkpoints 100/300/1,000). At measured costs this is \u2248 92 h of accelerator wall time against the 54,000 s envelope of plan 9; the envelope is therefore superseded by this decision and the ceilings are set from the measured components (R1-55, endpoint runs). The orchestrator's 48-cell proposal (lead queue 20) is withdrawn. | `docs/lead_queue.md` items 20, 22. | Lead: \"don't cut the scope please\". |",
      "sha256": "8379f07f832c51a421578205477795a45c726dd1c63f7fe6b085c9a330f155e8"
    },
    {
      "row": "| DEC-045 | 2026-09-14 | **MQuAKE-CF is the third confirmatory dataset** (lead: \"i approve MQuAKE-CF -- please download -- i would also rather keep CounterFact and add MQuAKE as a third dataset\"). Downloaded to `assets/data/raw/mquake/` (MIT; upstream commit `a4f38bb`; hashes in `manifests/datasets.json`). Single-hop rewrites become edit items (cloze prompt, question-form paraphrase, aliases from `new_single_hops`); the multi-hop questions become the verified composition inventory. 6,043 unique rewrites on subjects outside register v3. CounterFact stays in the matrix, which requires the DEC-042 exception (strict v3 leaves no CounterFact items); the run matrix gains a dataset axis value (360 cells). | `manifests/datasets.json`; `docs/ongoing.md` lane R1-D4. | Lead decision. |",
      "sha256": "4312cfa4e762b2d033126869f6f4d1c0edfc1e43ca7a67c93489e92795516e07"
    },
    {
      "row": "| DEC-046 (proposed default) | 2026-09-14 | **MQuAKE development slice and training pool**: from the 6,043 teacher-eligible items (`mquake_pool_v1.json`; 0 teacher-correct, as expected for counterfactual targets) a 200-item development slice (`manifests/dev/mquake_dev.json`) and a 500-item training pool (`train_pool_mquake_v1.json`), seed 46, one item per subject, disjoint, with the 159 zsRE-overlap subjects left to the zsRE side; the reader is retrained on three pools (CounterFact 1,000 + zsRE 1,000 + MQuAKE 500) so the MQuAKE claim has the same same-source form as the other two datasets. Sizes chosen for yield: \u2248 5,150 items remain for the confirmatory reservations (\u2248 4,050 needed). The lead may choose transfer-only (no MQuAKE training) instead. | `scripts/r1_d5_mquake_teacher.py`, `scripts/r1_d6_mquake_split.py`. | Proposed by the orchestrator under DEC-045. |",
      "sha256": "54e0a2bc07cbb6bf2df8159e4538a44204334cb2182335364ae0390ab0b543b7"
    },
    {
      "row": "| DEC-047 (accepted 2026-09-15: lead \"Q2 yes\") | 2026-09-14 | **S1_LM certified**: the informative LM continuation at weight lr 1e-8 (`r1_24_control_lm_v3_lr1e-8`) passes the pre-registered fidelity gate (KL 0.0005 nats \u2264 0.001; NLL \u22120.009) and is the S1_LM base for the matrix; lr 1e-6 (v2) stays on record as the failed-gate run. U03 closes by data; no scope amendment needed. | `docs/R1_stage2_notes.md` (R1-24 follow-up); `results/R1/r1_24/r1_24_lm_v3_lr1e-8/`. | Orchestrator under DEC-040; the lead may prefer the failed-gate labelling instead. |",
      "sha256": "6ce251695a08bf4084414db94938cd83e1175852582b2a6cd025868ad2798e42"
    },
    {
      "row": "| DEC-048 | 2026-09-15 | **MQuAKE population: option C** (lead: \"option C please instead of your default choice of A\"): a locality or unrelated-query presentation of a subject's TRUE fact during reader training or development evaluation is not exposure for a later COUNTERFACTUAL edit of that subject. The exclusion register's query-role reasons are waived for MQuAKE (primary training/development items, sealed/drawn items and every other reason stay); capacity 4,218 distinct subjects against 4,050 needed (R1-D7 option C count) before alias/context clearance \u2014 the draw must abort if clearance drops it below demand. The 360-cell matrix at 1,000 edits stands. | `docs/tasks/R1-D7.md` \u00a7Option C; `docs/lead_queue.md` 27\u201328. | Lead decision; recorded as the register policy v5 (lane R1-D1h). The report must state the reading explicitly. |",
      "sha256": "c03c5b0b26ec053eaddc09bd7941bb5cbaf64b990f22cf24ee31c6a194f7faa2"
    }
